  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 202 AM MDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nSmoke continues to be the main impact across Eastern Idaho to start \nthe new week. The weak trough passing through Montana early this \nmorning will bring a drop in our temperatures, but will also \ncontinue bringing breezy winds through the morning hours. Wind gusts \nthrough the morning stay around 15 to 20 mph with gusts to 25 mph \nthrough parts of the eastern Magic Valley and upper Snake River \nPlain. Winds begin to drop off during the afternoon and will be \nlight overnight into Tuesday morning. While patchy smoke will \npersist throughout today, we will likely see an increase in smoke \nimpacts overnight into Tuesday morning as winds get even lighter and \nparticles are able to settle out of the atmosphere a bit more. Highs \ntoday will be in the upper 70s to low 80s across much of the area, a \ncool down behind the weak cold front passing through, and this \n\"cooler\" weather will continue on Tuesday, but highs will be back \ninto the upper 80s and low 90s by Wednesday afternoon. The ridge of \nhigh pressure builds in over the West again in the second half of \nthe weekend which means highs will be back into the 90s and low \ntriple digits by Friday. There is basically zero precipitation in \nthe forecast this week, with hot, dry, breezy conditions continuing \nto bring near-critical fire weather conditions to the area \nthroughout the week.",
